LOTS Client Side Trade Services - Updated Reference Guide
Rule 1: There are 8 active products used by Lloyds
1. Import Letter of Credit (ILC)

2. Export Letter of Credit (ELC)

3. Import Collection (IC)

4. Export Collection (EC)

5. Undertaking Issuance (UI)

6. Undertaking Advised (UA)

7. Standby LC Issuance (SBLC-I)

8. Standby LC Advised (SBLC-A)
Rule 2 (Very Important)
Products customers can initiate from LOTS (Fresh Transaction)

These 4 can be created directly by customers.

✓ Import Letter of Credit

✓ Export Collection

✓ Undertaking Issuance

✓ Standby LC Issuance

Think:

Customer is requesting Lloyds to do something.

Example
Product	Customer says
Import LC	Please issue an LC for my import
Export Collection	Please collect payment from buyer
Undertaking Issuance	Please issue a guarantee
Standby LC Issuance	Please issue an SBLC
Products that originate from TI (Back office)

These cannot be freshly initiated from LOTS.

✗ Export Letter of Credit

✗ Import Collection

✗ Undertaking Advised

✗ Standby LC Advised

These start from TI/back-office.

Then LOTS customer can view/manage/respond.

Think:

Bank is informing the customer.

Example
Product	Who initiates?	Customer receives
Export LC	Other bank/TI	LC received
Import Collection	Exporter bank/TI	Collection documents received
Undertaking Advised	Other bank/TI	Guarantee received
Standby LC Advised	Other bank/TI	SBLC received
